usage: cairn doctor [-h] [--db PATH] [--bundle PATH] [--pin PATH]
                    [--attest PATH] [--log LEVEL] [--json] [--fix]
                    [--root PATH] [--dry-run] [--quick] [--only SUBSYSTEM,...]
                    [--online] [--explain FINDING-ID] [--robot-triage]
                    SUBCOMMAND ...

diagnose the M0 deploy shape read-only, and repair the two failure modes it
owns with --fix

positional arguments:
  SUBCOMMAND
    undo                restore every file a run changed, in reverse order,
                        from its verbatim backups
    capabilities        print the doctor contract: detectors, fixers, exit
                        codes, artifact layout
    health              one line and an exit code; the cheap detectors only
    robot-docs          print the doctor's agent handbook
    ls                  list the runs recorded in
                        .doctor/scorecard_history.jsonl

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --db PATH             substrate SQLite file
  --bundle PATH         gate bundle SQLite file
  --pin PATH            gate-bundle pin file
  --attest PATH         attestation file
  --log LEVEL           log level for the JSON records on stderr
  --json, --robot       emit exactly one JSON document on stdout
  --fix                 required for the irreversible part of this command
  --root PATH           checkout root: locates .doctor/, .gitignore,
                        pyproject.toml and .git/HEAD
  --dry-run             with --fix, print the plan and write only the run
                        artifact
  --quick               cheap detectors only: no gp spawn, no KAT
  --only SUBSYSTEM,...  scope to a subset of subsystems: deploy, dirs, gates,
                        gp, pari, project, substrate
  --online              enable network probes; refused at M0, nothing needs
                        one
  --explain FINDING-ID  expand one finding with its evidence
  --robot-triage        one JSON document: summary, findings, actions_planned,
                        recommended_command

Structured output: add --json to any read-side command. Contract: cairn
capabilities --json. Agent handbook: cairn robot-docs.
